[center]
[size=6][b][color=#42ACC8]Skyrim Vanity System[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#F5F5F5]Native in-game transmog and vanity outfit management for Skyrim[/color][/size]

[color=#F5F5F5]Keep your real equipped gear for gameplay while changing the visible appearance through a fast native browser, preview tools, and a condition-aware variant workbench.[/color]

[b][color=#D19349]Requires [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/175181]Dynamic Armor Variants Extended[/url][/color][/b] to function.

[b][color=#42ACC8]Default hotkey:[/color][/b] [b][color=#F5F5F5]F6[/color][/b]
[i][color=#9B9B9B]Configurable in the UI or in settings.json.[/color][/i]
[/center]

[hr]

[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]What It Is[/color][/b][/size]

Skyrim Vanity System is a player-facing transmog system for Skyrim.

It separates [i]gameplay equipment[/i] from [i]visible appearance[/i], so you can keep the armor you actually want for stats and enchantments while presenting a completely different look in-game.

It is built around a native SKSE + Dear ImGui interface designed for fast iteration: browse gear, outfits, slots, and kits in one place, preview before committing, apply item or slot overrides, build conditional rules in-game, and target yourself or NPCs directly.

[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]Highlights[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Live preview workflow[/b] for gear, outfits, and kits before applying changes[/*]
[*][b]Item-based and slot-based overrides[/b] for both precise and broad appearance control[/*]
[*][b]Searchable browser[/b] for individual armor pieces, outfits, and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/137877]Modex[/url] kits[/*]
[*][b]Condition editor[/b] for building context-sensitive appearance rules in-game[/*]
[*][b]NPC targeting[/b] by opening the menu while focused on another actor[/*]
[*][b]Favorites, persistence, and Modex-style presentation[/b] built into the native UI[/*]
[/list]

